„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„For which cause both thou and all thy company are gathered together against the LORD: and what is Aaron, that ye murmur against him?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And Moses sent to call Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab: which said, We will not come up:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´is it a small thing that thou hast brought us up out of a land that floweth with milk and honey, to kill us in the wilderness, except thou make thyself altogether a prince over us?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾Moreover thou hast not brought us into a land that floweth with milk and honey, or given us inheritance of fields and vineyards: wilt thou put out the eyes of these men? we will not come up.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—And Moses was very wroth, and said unto the LORD, Respect not thou their offering: I have not taken one ass from them, neither have I hurt one of them.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd Moses said unto Korah, Be thou and all thy company before the LORD, thou, and they, and Aaron, to morrow:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·and take every man his censer, and put incense in them, and bring ye before the LORD every man his censer, two hundred and fifty censers; thou also, and Aaron, each of you his censer.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And they took every man his censer, and put fire in them, and laid incense thereon, and stood in the door of the tabernacle of the congregation with Moses and Aaron.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And Korah gathered all the congregation against them unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation: and the glory of the LORD appeared unto all the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVSeparate yourselves from among this congregation, that I may consume them in a moment.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšAnd they fell upon their faces, and said, O God, the God of the spirits of all flesh, shall one man sin, and wilt thou be wroth with all the congregation?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgSpeak unto the congregation, saying, Get you up from about the tabernacle of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd Moses rose up and went unto Dathan and Abiram; and the elders of Israel followed him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨And he spake unto the congregation, saying, Depart, I pray you, from the tents of these wicked men, and touch nothing of their's, lest ye be consumed in all their sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑSo they gat up from the tabernacle of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram, on every side: and Dathan and Abiram came out, and stood in the door of their tents, and their wives, and their sons, and their little children.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Moses said, Hereby ye shall know that the LORD hath sent me to do all these works; for I have not done them of mine own mind.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„If these men die the common death of all men, or if they be visited after the visitation of all men; then the LORD hath not sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÜBut if the LORD make a new thing, and the earth open her mouth, and swallow them up, with all that appertain unto them, and they go down quick into the pit; then ye shall understand that these men have provoked the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzAnd it came to pass, as he had made an end of speaking all these words, that the ground clave asunder that was under them:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠand the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed them up, and their houses, and all the men that appertained unto Korah, and all their goods.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”They, and all that appertained to them, went down alive into the pit, and the earth closed upon them: and they perished from among the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd all Israel that were round about them fled at the cry of them: for they said, Lest the earth swallow us up also.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiAnd there came out a fire from the LORD, and consumed the two hundred and fifty men that offered incense.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse(¦verses•„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜Speak unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, that he take up the censers out of the burning, and scatter thou the fire yonder; for they are hallowed.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìThe censers of these sinners against their own souls, let them make them broad plates for a covering of the altar: for they offered them before the LORD, therefore they are hallowed: and they shall be a sign unto the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜And Eleazar the priest took the brasen censers, wherewith they that were burnt had offered; and they were made broad plates for a covering of the altar:¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙéto be a memorial unto the children of Israel, that no stranger, which is not of the seed of Aaron, come near to offer incense before the LORD; that he be not as Korah, and as his company: as the LORD said to him by the hand of Moses.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse-¦verses•„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™But on the morrow all the congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and against Aaron, saying, Ye have killed the people of the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÛAnd it came to pass, when the congregation was gathered against Moses and against Aaron, that they looked toward the tabernacle of the congregation: and, behold, the cloud covered it, and the glory of the LORD appeared.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd Moses and Aaron came before the tabernacle of the congregation.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ&And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpGet you up from among this congregation, that I may consume them as in a moment. And they fell upon their faces.¦layout ªlast_verse-…¤book§chapter«first_verse.ªlast_verse2¦verses•„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙìAnd Moses said unto Aaron, Take a censer, and put fire therein from off the altar, and put on incense, and go quickly unto the congregation, and make an atonement for them: for there is wrath gone out from the LORD; the plague is begun.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿And Aaron took as Moses commanded, and ran into the midst of the congregation; and, behold, the plague was begun among the people: and he put on incense, and made an atonement for the people.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd he stood between the dead and the living; and the plague was stayed.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Now they 